INSERT INTO `cleaned_signal` VALUES ('clean_bf4b52afd2524b4aa2f5c8935731969d', 'signal_1c1850629de74c76ba62ec77cd8a0001', 'How do Saviynt runbooks and automation workflows work in real-world scenarios? How do Saviynt runbooks and automation workflows work in real-world scenarios? How do Saviynt runbooks and automation workflows work in real-world scenarios? I’m currently exploring Saviynt Identity Cloud and trying to gain a deeper, practical understanding of how its runbooks, triggers, and automation capabilities work in real-world enterprise environments. From the official documentation, I understand that Saviynt provides strong support for identity lifecycle management (provisioning, deprovisioning, access requests, and governance). However, I’m specifically interested in going beyond the high-level concepts and understanding how these automation features are actually designed, configured, and executed in practice. I would really appreciate insights into the following areas: 🔹 Runbooks & Automation Design How are runbooks defined in Saviynt? Are they configured purely via UI workflows, or is there a way to define them programmatically (JSON/config-based)? What is the underlying execution model (task engine, workflow engine, job orchestration)? How are multi-step automations handled? For example: onboarding → role assignment → approval → provisioning → notification Is there support for conditional branching, retries, and error handling? 🔹 Trigger Mechanisms What types of triggers are supported in real implementations? Event-driven (e.g., user created/updated in HR system) Scheduled jobs (batch-based processing) Approval-based triggers (post-access request approval) API/webhook-driven triggers How does Saviynt handle near real-time vs batch-based execution? 🔹 Integration Capabilities How are integrations typically implemented with systems like: Active Directory / Azure AD (Entra ID) Cloud platforms (AWS, Azure) ITSM tools (ServiceNow, Jira) Are these integrations handled via: Out-of-the-box connectors REST APIs Custom connectors or middleware layers? 🔹 Scripting & Extensibility Is it possible to embed or invoke scripts (e.g., PowerShell, Python) within workflows or runbooks? Can Saviynt call external automation services (e.g., Azure Functions, Logic Apps, Lambda)? How flexible is the platform when implementing custom business logic? 🔹 Enterprise Customization & Best Practices How customizable are workflows for complex enterprise scenarios (RBAC/ABAC, approval chains, exception handling)? What are common architectural patterns used in production deployments? Any best practices for: Scaling automation Managing failures/retries Ensuring auditability and compliance? If anyone has hands-on experience, architectural diagrams, or real-world implementation examples, I’d love to learn from your insights. Thanks in advance! Stack Overflow query: feature request process https://stackoverflow.com/questions/[phone]/how-do-saviynt-runbooks-and-automation-workflows-work-in-real-world-scenarios', 'How do Saviynt runbooks and automation workflows work in real-world scenarios', '[\"how\", \"in\", \"are\", \"automation\", \"saviynt\", \"real\", \"runbooks\", \"workflows\"]', 'positive', 4, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 0.90, 'v1');
