INSERT INTO `cleaned_signal` VALUES ('clean_c711db523bfd49d4a7a89810b6f686c5', 'signal_cd516a80f74f49f980197e379dfca412', '[dead] [dead] [dead] I follow ~50 YouTube channels for work (tech, finance, geopolitics). I was spending more time scanning my subscription feed than actually watching anything useful. Built Rundown to fix this for myself. How it works: connect your Google account, pick channels, get a daily email with structured summaries and timestamps for every new upload. Uses WebSub for real-time upload detection and Gemini Flash for multimodal analysis (it reads visuals too, not just transcripts). Each summary includes key points with clickable timestamps and a \"worth watching if...\" recommendation so you can decide in 30 seconds whether a 45-minute video deserves your time. Stack: Fastify, WebSub, Gemini 3 Flash, Railway. Known limitations: summary quality varies with video structure — works well for structured educational content, worse for rambly vlogs. Search across past summaries isn&#x27;t built yet. YouTube only, no podcasts. Happy to answer questions about the architecture FAQ Q: Is this just another wrapper? A: Depends on your perspective. The idea was to provide value to people who don&#x27;t want to setup manual workflows, get a Gemini Subscription, use some emailing solution. Maybe a technical person can set this up with their existing subscriptions but for many users, it&#x27;s an all-in-one solution for research. Q: If it builds the summaries, then why would someone watch the video? Wouldn&#x27;t it hurt the creators? A: No. The entire idea was to keep the summaries to a very high level and not essentially provide a transcript of the video. We still want to drive traffic to actual content creators but this is a filter for people to decide where to spend the next few mins&#x2F;hours. Hacker News comment query: manual workflow https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=[phone]', '[dead] [dead] [dead] I follow ~50 YouTube channels for work (tech, finance, geopolitics). I was spending more time scan…', '[\"to\", \"it\", \"summaries\", \"video\", \"x27\", \"dead\", \"gemini\", \"time\"]', 'neutral', 2, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 0.90, 'v1');
