INSERT INTO `cleaned_signal` VALUES ('clean_ddb32ba52eb7443f9a9e76ad267c46b8', 'signal_135d2b9d821f4b8e85b61432185172b1', 'Is this Deep Learning → GenAI roadmap (project-based) sufficient for transitioning into LLM & GenAI engineering in 2026? Is this Deep Learning → GenAI roadmap (project-based) sufficient for transitioning into LLM & GenAI engineering in 2026? Is this Deep Learning → GenAI roadmap (project-based) sufficient for transitioning into LLM & GenAI engineering in 2026? I\'m a Computer Science student building a project-based learning path to transition from Deep Learning to Generative AI / LLM Engineering. My learning approach is: Learn concepts only when required by a project Start with classical DL → NLP → Transformers → GenAI → MLOps Use a Fake News Detection system as a long-running project that evolves with each phase This is a high-level overview of my roadmap (details omitted for brevity): Phase 1 – Deep Learning Core Linear algebra, gradients, backprop intuition Dense neural networks, activation & loss functions Optimizers (Adam/AdamW), regularization Project: Basic Fake News Classifier (TF-IDF / NN) Phase 2 – NLP Foundations TF-IDF vs embeddings (Word2Vec, GloVe) RNNs, LSTMs, sequence modeling Project upgrade: Bi-LSTM-based fake news detection Phase 3 – Transformers Self-attention, positional encoding, multi-head attention BERT fine-tuning for classification Tokenization (BPE, WordPiece) Project upgrade: Transformer-based classifier Phase 4 – Computer Vision & Multimodality CNNs, transfer learning Vision Transformers, CLIP Fake image/news consistency checks Phase 5 – Generative AI & LLM Engineering LLM fine-tuning (LoRA / QLoRA) Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Vector databases Agent-based workflows Project extension: News verification chatbot with explanations Phase 6 – System Design & MLOps FastAPI inference Docker, Kubernetes Model monitoring & optimization Scalable GenAI system design Questions Is this roadmap technically sound for transitioning from Deep Learning into GenAI / LLM engineering roles? Are there critical gaps (e.g., evaluation, inference optimization, data-centric AI) that I should add? Any ordering changes you would recommend based on real-world industry practice? I\'m especially interested in feedback from people working with LLMs, production ML systems, or applied GenAI. Thanks in advance Stack Overflow query: product feedback workflow https://stackoverflow.com/questions/[phone]/is-this-deep-learning-%e2%86%92-genai-roadmap-project-based-sufficient-for-transitioni', 'Is this Deep Learning → GenAI roadmap (project-based) sufficient for transitioning into LLM & GenAI engineering in 2026', '[\"genai\", \"project\", \"learning\", \"based\", \"deep\", \"is\", \"llm\", \"phase\"]', 'positive', 2, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 0.90, 'v1');
INSERT INTO `cleaned_signal` VALUES ('clean_df2cd8935467426aa2803ed42f90b712', 'signal_ada5ce412b2949c0ae7a7c90d1d074a1', 'How to convince team other parts of software development are important? How to convince team other parts of software development are important? How to convince team other parts of software development are important? Sometimes, when I present a part of the software development process to certain people, say the supervisor or the manager that they don\'t have experience say Automated unit tests and integration tests vs. their manual functional testing. Using code generators, and scripts for repetitive tasks. I sometimes met with resistance. Some of the reasons are the following: They say that that\'s the way we do things here. Our system works and there is no need to add in our process. They are busy being busy. They say is their job is to get us projects and our job is to deliver it to them to their satisfaction. They are satisfied when if it is a manual system, repetitive but on time. They are very conservative about code generators. I gave them an estimate that it takes a significant time overhead for the first project to use this and time to train my teammates since this approach is relatively new to them. The overhead for the first project to them overshadows the benefit in the long run, but I explained the convenience it is to us developers, but they are always stuck to do things the old way. What would be your strategy for this? Stack Overflow query: repetitive task automation https://stackoverflow.com/questions/903513/how-to-convince-team-other-parts-of-software-development-are-important', 'Sometimes, when I present a part of the software development process to certain people, say the supervisor or the manag…', '[\"to\", \"are\", \"is\", \"they\", \"of\", \"development\", \"software\", \"convince\"]', 'neutral', 3, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1.00, 'v1');
INSERT INTO `cleaned_signal` VALUES ('clean_e488e225dcca452887d2ce4f80f150ce', 'signal_b1a49a54bb5e4312a7f335bf1c28c177', 'How can I generate the OpenAPI arbitrary type using Swagger Core (springdoc-openapi)? How can I generate the OpenAPI arbitrary type using Swagger Core (springdoc-openapi)? How can I generate the OpenAPI arbitrary type using Swagger Core (springdoc-openapi)? I am working on an application which uses the springdoc-openapi library to generate OpenAPI v3 endpoints for its Spring controllers. This library uses Swagger Core for the actual mapping of Java Objects to OpenAPI schemas. There is a request/response type used by a controller which includes a property of type . This type can therefore be any of the data types defined by OpenAPI: , , , , , or . Note that is a distinct type from the other types; e.g. a or is not an . The OpenAPI 3.0 Specification specifies that a schema without any type will match any data type. A schema without a type matches any data type – numbers, strings, objects, and so on. A proper way to model this, then, would be the following Swagger definition, where there is no property for : However, per open issue swagger-core#3834 , Java values are mapped to OpenAPI types, not an arbitrary type. As noted above, this means that it would be incorrect for such an API to return or accept a type that is not an OpenAPI , such as a , , , etc. I made various attempts to get the application to generate this type as the OpenAPI arbitrary type, but to no avail. One thing I discovered when playing around with using a custom to use a Swagger with a null is that ends up converting the type to as part of its internal processing. This is currently documented as an open feature request of Swagger Core as swagger-core#4014 . With this all being said: how can I get my generated type to use the OpenAPI arbitrary type? Stack Overflow query: feature request process https://stackoverflow.com/questions/[phone]/how-can-i-generate-the-openapi-arbitrary-type-using-swagger-core-springdoc-open', 'e.g. a or is not an . The OpenAPI 3.0 Specification specifies that a schema without any type will match any data type. …', '[\"type\", \"openapi\", \"to\", \"swagger\", \"core\", \"arbitrary\", \"is\", \"an\"]', 'neutral', 3, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1.00, 'v1');
