INSERT INTO `cleaned_signal` VALUES ('clean_e72160d7fb84427c84e80c54b8bc734b', 'signal_a719438bb8ce4ede8ca33888f9fc60e1', 'Automating repetitive tasks with Ruby and Selenium WebDriver Automating repetitive tasks with Ruby and Selenium WebDriver Automating repetitive tasks with Ruby and Selenium WebDriver I followed the advice from this question and I started to experimenting with Selenium, but I feel like it has to many limitations. Could you recommend something more suitable? A simple program that sends data to a website would be ideal. EDIT// Soooo apparently Selenium will be enough for me. I just need to upgrade it a little. Here is a code I wrote so far ( EDIT2// outdated. I will post updated code below) Suprisingly, it works. But I want it to work better. I would like a window to appear where I could scan serial numbers and type login and password (with \'remember me\' option). Ideally It would look this: EDIT2// When I\'m talking about window, I have something like THAT in mind. Also I\'ve been searching for solutions and I find THIS . I think it will be what I\'m looking for. \"Scan serial number\" means the user has to scan like 4 to 7 hundreds serial numbers per day. It wouldn\'t be bad, BUT as I explained in previous question (link at the begining) it is very time consuming. Here are the steps the user needs to follow: Logging in Select workstation Scan serial number (redirect to next website) Marks him as good or bad (If good fault code = 1, if bad, fault code according to malfunction. That why I need dropdown wit fault codes list) Confirm (redirect to previous website) Go back to step 3 for next serial number As You can see, there is a lot of clicking. What I want to achieve is: Scan multiple serial numbers. Each one goes to separate row, where I can select fault code for this specific serial number (that\'s why I need dropdown with fault codes) Send them all at once and let Selenium do all the clicking. So far I manage to run Beta version, that is working. I run batch file with following code: Here is updated code for Selenium automation (test.rb): Even though it works as intended, I\'m running into some errors. Every instance may cause error, cause sometime the website is slow AF and I get \"NoSuchElementException\" because page didn\'t load in time for element to be present. I know that Selenium has something like but I didn\'t manage to get it to work yet Stack Overflow query: repetitive task automation https://stackoverflow.com/questions/[phone]/automating-repetitive-tasks-with-ruby-and-selenium-webdriver', 'A simple program that sends data to a website would be ideal. EDIT// Soooo apparently Selenium will be enough for me. I…', '[\"to\", \"it\", \"selenium\", \"code\", \"is\", \"serial\", \"be\", \"fault\"]', 'negative', 4, 0, NULL, 0, 1, 1.00, 'v1');
