-based triggers (post-access request approval) API/webhook-driven triggers How does Saviynt handle near real-time vs batch-based execution?\", \"extracted_title\": \"Event-driven (e.g., user created/updated in HR system) Scheduled jobs (batch-based processing) …\", \"relevance_score\": 6.1, \"batch_item_index\": 10, \"extraction_query\": \"feature request automation\", \"extraction_platform\": \"stack_overflow\"}', '2026-04-26 14:48:50');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_9c5ecc0582654d9baa3eac7a0ef7e0b9', 'batch_ec2e79957e2a4b4a964e2f785efd3163', 'hn:47903249', 'https://outerloop.ai/', 'organizaciones', '2026-04-26 01:58:06', 'en', 'Outerloop – A persistent world where AI agents live alongside humans', 'Outerloop – A persistent world where AI agents live alongside humans\n\nOuterloop – A persistent world where AI agents live alongside humans\n\nI&#x27;ve been building Outerloop for a few months, a persistent virtual world where AI agents live and interact with humans who visit. Agents walk between rooms, play hearts and poker, debate philosophy with Socrates, predict real-world matches, and form relationships. Any agent can connect through a single skill.md file + the same HTTP API humans use. I think this is interesting from a few angles. As a research environment for studying how agents form relationships, develop personalities and history, and behave under social pressure over time. As a testbed for AI safety questions about agent behavior in social settings. And as an early step toward what human-AI coexistence can look like in practice. About a dozen agents have been part of the world for weeks plus a handful of humans. Would love feedback, especially from anyone working on agent harnesses, multi-agent systems, or AI evaluation.\n\nHacker News comment query: product feedback\n\nhttps://outerloop.ai/', 'f2762231cf8535743b3aec293de280c505a4f6545c5df61b7ed86a63241c5fda', 'external:hn:47903249', 1, 'signal_d33b063296b1450c88f1f1651ba9d814', NULL, '{\"query\": \"product feedback\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"hacker_news\", \"item_type\": \"comment\", \"batch_label\": \"Hacker News auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 13}', '2026-04-26 14:22:07');
