won\'t work since the data I need to scrape is loaded dynamically by JavaScript after the initial page load.\", \"extracted_title\": \"This is frustrating because I need Selenium to handle the JavaScript-rendered content on the pa…\", \"relevance_score\": 4.9, \"batch_item_index\": 12, \"extraction_query\": \"feature request automation\", \"extraction_platform\": \"stack_overflow\"}', '2026-04-26 14:40:07');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_cba18288f9be404d96efba4a24d5d8df', 'batch_a328b84cba50480da5656ace9cb1608d', 'so:79919190', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79919190/how-to-automatically-install-latest-python-package-versions-in-aws-mwaa-from-s3', 'Hrithik Hiranwar', '2026-04-03 01:01:51', 'en', 'How to automatically install latest Python package versions in AWS MWAA from S3 requirements.txt without manual updates?', 'How to automatically install latest Python package versions in AWS MWAA from S3 requirements.txt without manual updates?\n\nHow to automatically install latest Python package versions in AWS MWAA from S3 requirements.txt without manual updates?\n\nBody: I am using AWS Managed Workflows for Apache Airflow (MWAA) where the file is stored in an S3 bucket and MWAA syncs it during environment updates. Current Setup: is uploaded to S3 MWAA environment installs dependencies from this file Any update to the file in S3 triggers dependency installation My Requirement: I want a fully automated setup where: I upload a to S3 (even once) MWAA always installs the latest available versions of packages automatically No manual intervention is required (no version pinning or editing file repeatedly) For example: Expected Behavior: Whenever MWAA processes the from S3: It should always fetch and install the latest versions of all listed packages from PyPI Concerns / Questions: Does MWAA always install the latest versions when no version is specified, or does it cache previously installed versions? If packages are already installed, will MWAA re-install newer versions automatically on S3 updates? Is there any mechanism in MWAA to force dependency refresh/reinstall from S3 without modifying the file? Are there any AWS-recommended patterns (e.g., dynamic versioning, CI/CD automation, or lifecycle hooks) to achieve this behavior? Goal: To avoid manually updating for every new package version and have a hands-off dependency management system in MWAA, especially for POC or dynamic environments. Any guidance or real-world experience with this would be really helpful. Thanks!\n\nStack Overflow query: manual workflow automation\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/79919190/how-to-automatically-install-latest-python-package-versions-in-aws-mwaa-from-s3', 'cf19b9f5cb2a99279098ccdeb008c86e34c3111392dbde5ba1ef5825eeb0f336', 'external:so:79919190', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"airflow\", \"mwaa\", \"aws-airflow-mwaa\"], \"query\": \"manual workflow automation\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 3}', '2026-04-26 14:20:00');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_cd516a80f74f49f980197e379dfca412', 'batch_79e0afe62cda4b9fb55d5eb4f5ada6f7', 'hn:47868872', 'https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47868872', 'razasaad92', '2026-04-23 04:27:55', 'en', '[dead]', '[dead]\n\n[dead]\n\nI follow ~50 YouTube channels for work (tech, finance, geopolitics). I was spending more time scanning my subscription feed than actually watching anything useful. Built Rundown to fix this for myself. How it works: connect your Google account, pick channels, get a daily email with structured summaries and timestamps for every new upload. Uses WebSub for real-time upload detection and Gemini Flash for multimodal analysis (it reads visuals too, not just transcripts). Each summary includes key points with clickable timestamps and a \"worth watching if...\" recommendation so you can decide in 30 seconds whether a 45-minute video deserves your time. Stack: Fastify, WebSub, Gemini 3 Flash, Railway. Known limitations: summary quality varies with video structure — works well for structured educational content, worse for rambly vlogs. Search across past summaries isn&#x27;t built yet. YouTube only, no podcasts. Happy to answer questions about the architecture FAQ Q: Is this just another wrapper? A: Depends on your perspective. The idea was to provide value to people who don&#x27;t want to setup manual workflows, get a Gemini Subscription, use some emailing solution. Maybe a technical person can set this up with their existing subscriptions but for many users, it&#x27;s an all-in-one solution for research. Q: If it builds the summaries, then why would someone watch the video? Wouldn&#x27;t it hurt the creators? A: No. The entire idea was to keep the summaries to a very high level and not essentially provide a transcript of the video. We still want to drive traffic to actual content creators but this is a filter for people to decide where to spend the next few mins&#x2F;hours.\n\nHacker News comment query: manual workflow\n\nhttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47868872', 'af127ed9061db161713270499b78a2b995c3cde07361ec0cda0ccbe9e8646a89', 'external:hn:47868872', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"query\": \"manual workflow\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"hacker_news\", \"item_type\": \"comment\", \"batch_label\": \"Hacker News auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 2}', '2026-04-26 14:19:59');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_cd555800cdcd4e6089de51bf9bdd6bc8', 'batch_ec2e79957e2a4b4a964e2f785efd3163', 'hn:47906916', 'https://github.com/niri-wm/niri/releases/tag/v26.04', 'likeclockwork', '2026-04-26 11:08:15', 'en', 'Niri 26.04: Scrollable-tiling Wayland compositor', 'Niri 26.04: Scrollable-tiling Wayland compositor\n\nNiri 26.04: Scrollable-tiling Wayland compositor\n\nThat&#x27;s not actually tiling, is it? To me that reads like fullscreen with workspaces. If one uses a manual tiling window manager like i3 or sway and a large monitor one can divide the screen into separate work areas that each host multiple applications based on their role in one&#x27;s workflow and use less workspaces. Scrolling makes a similar but different workflow practical on small screens where flexibility matters.\n\nHacker News comment query: manual workflow\n\nhttps://github.com/niri-wm/niri/releases/tag/v26.04', 'f64d31bfa5ae0d48ab83cdae0df0e2ad84ea33985234a7f14047cf76704869fb', 'external:hn:47906916', 1, 'signal_58b82b53ad6a4805a12555afe802ae9a', NULL, '{\"query\": \"manual workflow\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"hacker_news\", \"item_type\": \"comment\", \"batch_label\": \"Hacker News auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 0}', '2026-04-26 14:22:07');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_cdf78f3f69f14b7e9de60aa88b55e292', 'batch_bb246fd3ee5b4067ac2085631eba6c60', 'hn:47902023', 'https://driggsby.com/blog/claude-code-routine-watch-my-finances', 'mbm', '2026-04-25 23:02:19', 'en', 'The support issue is less \"my code broke\" and more things like \"this institution isn&#x27;t ret…', 'The support issue is less \"my code broke\" and more things like \"this institution isn&#x27;t ret…\n\nExtracted demand: The support issue is less \"my code broke\" and more things like \"this institution isn&#x27;t ret…\nUser pain point: The support issue is less \"my code broke\" and more things like \"this institution isn&#x27;t returning what it should,\" or, \"I haven&#x27;t been approved yet by this institution that does manual revie…\nEvidence excerpt: Hey! Thanks for stopping by. Actually planning to do a full blog post on this topic soon (how to get started with Plaid). It was a bit of a process involving sales calls, contracts, security attestations, etc., but they…\nOriginal source title: Could a Claude Code routine watch my finances?\n\nHacker News Comments auto discovery query: manual process\n\nhttps://driggsby.com/blog/claude-code-routine-watch-my-finances', '8cfd080e670a73a696a9368186d6bafcbc39cec5a893225d84d6cafa61f8870f', 'external:hn:47902023', 1, 'signal_38e812b73b284ba7af6a1e2f449c721c', NULL, '{\"query\": \"manual process\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"hacker_news\", \"item_type\": \"comment\", \"batch_label\": \"Hacker News auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"auto_extracted\": true, \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"anchor_sentence\": \"The support issue is less \\\"my code broke\\\" and more things like \\\"this institution isn&#x27;t returning what it should,\\\" or, \\\"I haven&#x27;t been approved yet by this institution that does manual review.\\\" Overall, it&#x27;s been a pretty good experience!\", \"extracted_title\": \"The support issue is less \\\"my code broke\\\" and more things like \\\"this institution isn&#x27;t ret…\", \"relevance_score\": 6.5, \"batch_item_index\": 2, \"extraction_query\": \"manual process\", \"extraction_platform\": \"hacker_news\"}', '2026-04-26 16:57:40');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_ce539b6807384adb82749ea059a6c98c', 'batch_a328b84cba50480da5656ace9cb1608d', 'so:79919760', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79919760/github-actions-workflow-not-scheduling-schedule-trigger-not-appearing', 'Park YeJun', '2026-04-04 00:34:23', 'en', 'GitHub Actions workflow not scheduling (Schedule trigger not appearing)', 'GitHub Actions workflow not scheduling (Schedule trigger not appearing)\n\nGitHub Actions workflow not scheduling (Schedule trigger not appearing)\n\nI have developed a Python script and set up a GitHub Actions workflow ( ) to execute it daily at 7 AM KST (22:00 UTC) using a schedule. The issue is that the scheduled automation does not trigger at all. While the (manual trigger) works perfectly fine, there is no indication in the GitHub Actions UI that the workflow is \"scheduled.\" I have already verified the following: No typos in the YAML file. The workflow file is correctly pushed to the default branch ( ). Actions permissions are enabled in the repository settings. The file exists on the default branch. Despite this, the \"clock icon\" or the \"Scheduled\" status is missing from the Actions tab. Has anyone experienced this issue where manual triggers work but the cron schedule is completely ignored by GitHub? I also checked the API ( ) and the state is \'active\', but the \'schedule\' property is missing in the response.\n\nStack Overflow query: manual workflow automation\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/79919760/github-actions-workflow-not-scheduling-schedule-trigger-not-appearing', '612eee3ea5ce330575112bd49edc9a9e81b834b536c78a713d284140835c7969', 'external:so:79919760', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"github-actions\"], \"query\": \"manual workflow automation\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 0}', '2026-04-26 14:20:00');
