way to automate opening each of those Excel files and copy/pasting t…\", \"relevance_score\": 6.1, \"batch_item_index\": 0, \"extraction_query\": \"manual process automate\", \"extraction_platform\": \"stack_overflow\"}', '2026-04-26 14:36:38');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_e6ef49fe209c414686f00fb991edb435', 'batch_a328b84cba50480da5656ace9cb1608d', 'so:69257874', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/69257874/how-can-i-generate-the-openapi-arbitrary-type-using-swagger-core-springdoc-open', 'M. Justin', '2021-09-21 00:26:21', 'en', 'How can I generate the OpenAPI arbitrary type using Swagger Core (springdoc-openapi)?', 'How can I generate the OpenAPI arbitrary type using Swagger Core (springdoc-openapi)?\n\nHow can I generate the OpenAPI arbitrary type using Swagger Core (springdoc-openapi)?\n\nI am working on an application which uses the springdoc-openapi library to generate OpenAPI v3 endpoints for its Spring controllers. This library uses Swagger Core for the actual mapping of Java Objects to OpenAPI schemas. There is a request/response type used by a controller which includes a property of type . This type can therefore be any of the data types defined by OpenAPI: , , , , , or . Note that is a distinct type from the other types; e.g. a or is not an . The OpenAPI 3.0 Specification specifies that a schema without any type will match any data type. A schema without a type matches any data type – numbers, strings, objects, and so on. A proper way to model this, then, would be the following Swagger definition, where there is no property for : However, per open issue swagger-core#3834 , Java values are mapped to OpenAPI types, not an arbitrary type. As noted above, this means that it would be incorrect for such an API to return or accept a type that is not an OpenAPI , such as a , , , etc. I made various attempts to get the application to generate this type as the OpenAPI arbitrary type, but to no avail. One thing I discovered when playing around with using a custom to use a Swagger with a null is that ends up converting the type to as part of its internal processing. This is currently documented as an open feature request of Swagger Core as swagger-core#4014 . With this all being said: how can I get my generated type to use the OpenAPI arbitrary type?\n\nStack Overflow query: feature request process\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/69257874/how-can-i-generate-the-openapi-arbitrary-type-using-swagger-core-springdoc-open', 'b58344ce698f19ff684e43f17ad30762fbf6bcbced2204bf149b2578b3e91e0c', 'external:so:69257874', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"java\", \"spring-mvc\", \"openapi\", \"springdoc\", \"swagger-core\"], \"query\": \"feature request process\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 4}', '2026-04-26 14:20:00');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_e7327a2a3dce4af19656cea922327c2c', 'batch_ec2e79957e2a4b4a964e2f785efd3163', 'hn:47861348', 'https://github.blog/news-insights/company-news/changes-to-github-copilot-individual-plans/', 'specproc', '2026-04-22 18:04:42', 'en', 'Changes to GitHub Copilot individual plans', 'Changes to GitHub Copilot individual plans\n\nChanges to GitHub Copilot individual plans\n\nGreat. I, a small consultancy, have just spent the last month working out a workload that uses Opus 4.6 via VS Code to prep horrible, inconsistent, survey data for upload to a proprietary platform. Worked a treat with some light babysitting. It&#x27;s the sort of messy job that agents excel at. Decisions need to be made on free text data, translations done into multiple languages, ambiguity handled. I now need to recheck it still works with another model, which involves a lot of manual verification; and potentially move to Claude Code and pay more money I can ill afford right now. I&#x27;m not even clear from the post when this comes in, I&#x27;m guessing effective immediately. This really hammers home for me the point that we should not be renting our tools. My own dumb fault for trusting them, I will make sure to learn from this.\n\nHacker News comment query: manual workflow\n\nhttps://github.blog/news-insights/company-news/changes-to-github-copilot-individual-plans/', 'fd24b9e557a29237d3d56ab8c3d1ccdafa2e4f91d6ee64873d3d3023b05e6a8a', 'external:hn:47861348', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"query\": \"manual workflow\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"hacker_news\", \"item_type\": \"comment\", \"batch_label\": \"Hacker News auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 3}', '2026-04-26 14:22:07');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_e85ec7c01a4e4d239acc0c53a67e8e5f', 'batch_ec2e79957e2a4b4a964e2f785efd3163', 'hn:47868872', 'https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47868872', 'razasaad92', '2026-04-23 04:27:55', 'en', '[dead]', '[dead]\n\n[dead]\n\nI follow ~50 YouTube channels for work (tech, finance, geopolitics). I was spending more time scanning my subscription feed than actually watching anything useful. Built Rundown to fix this for myself. How it works: connect your Google account, pick channels, get a daily email with structured summaries and timestamps for every new upload. Uses WebSub for real-time upload detection and Gemini Flash for multimodal analysis (it reads visuals too, not just transcripts). Each summary includes key points with clickable timestamps and a \"worth watching if...\" recommendation so you can decide in 30 seconds whether a 45-minute video deserves your time. Stack: Fastify, WebSub, Gemini 3 Flash, Railway. Known limitations: summary quality varies with video structure — works well for structured educational content, worse for rambly vlogs. Search across past summaries isn&#x27;t built yet. YouTube only, no podcasts. Happy to answer questions about the architecture FAQ Q: Is this just another wrapper? A: Depends on your perspective. The idea was to provide value to people who don&#x27;t want to setup manual workflows, get a Gemini Subscription, use some emailing solution. Maybe a technical person can set this up with their existing subscriptions but for many users, it&#x27;s an all-in-one solution for research. Q: If it builds the summaries, then why would someone watch the video? Wouldn&#x27;t it hurt the creators? A: No. The entire idea was to keep the summaries to a very high level and not essentially provide a transcript of the video. We still want to drive traffic to actual content creators but this is a filter for people to decide where to spend the next few mins&#x2F;hours.\n\nHacker News comment query: manual workflow\n\nhttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47868872', 'af127ed9061db161713270499b78a2b995c3cde07361ec0cda0ccbe9e8646a89', 'external:hn:47868872', 1, 'signal_cd516a80f74f49f980197e379dfca412', NULL, '{\"query\": \"manual workflow\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"hacker_news\", \"item_type\": \"comment\", \"batch_label\": \"Hacker News auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 2}', '2026-04-26 14:22:07');
