-based triggers (post-access request approval) API/webhook-driven triggers How does Saviynt handle near real-time vs batch-based execution?\", \"extracted_title\": \"Event-driven (e.g., user created/updated in HR system) Scheduled jobs (batch-based processing) …\", \"relevance_score\": 6.1, \"batch_item_index\": 10, \"extraction_query\": \"feature request automation\", \"extraction_platform\": \"stack_overflow\"}', '2026-04-26 14:47:47');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_f9b79a7fa87f4d17a1abe070f4a11e5c', 'batch_a328b84cba50480da5656ace9cb1608d', 'so:79909426', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79909426/automating-repetitive-tasks-with-ruby-and-selenium-webdriver', 'Shruikan', '2026-03-18 00:42:27', 'en', 'Automating repetitive tasks with Ruby and Selenium WebDriver', 'Automating repetitive tasks with Ruby and Selenium WebDriver\n\nAutomating repetitive tasks with Ruby and Selenium WebDriver\n\nI followed the advice from this question and I started to experimenting with Selenium, but I feel like it has to many limitations. Could you recommend something more suitable? A simple program that sends data to a website would be ideal. EDIT// Soooo apparently Selenium will be enough for me. I just need to upgrade it a little. Here is a code I wrote so far ( EDIT2// outdated. I will post updated code below) Suprisingly, it works. But I want it to work better. I would like a window to appear where I could scan serial numbers and type login and password (with \'remember me\' option). Ideally It would look this: EDIT2// When I\'m talking about window, I have something like THAT in mind. Also I\'ve been searching for solutions and I find THIS . I think it will be what I\'m looking for. \"Scan serial number\" means the user has to scan like 4 to 7 hundreds serial numbers per day. It wouldn\'t be bad, BUT as I explained in previous question (link at the begining) it is very time consuming. Here are the steps the user needs to follow: Logging in Select workstation Scan serial number (redirect to next website) Marks him as good or bad (If good fault code = 1, if bad, fault code according to malfunction. That why I need dropdown wit fault codes list) Confirm (redirect to previous website) Go back to step 3 for next serial number As You can see, there is a lot of clicking. What I want to achieve is: Scan multiple serial numbers. Each one goes to separate row, where I can select fault code for this specific serial number (that\'s why I need dropdown with fault codes) Send them all at once and let Selenium do all the clicking. So far I manage to run Beta version, that is working. I run batch file with following code: Here is updated code for Selenium automation (test.rb): Even though it works as intended, I\'m running into some errors. Every instance may cause error, cause sometime the website is slow AF and I get \"NoSuchElementException\" because page didn\'t load in time for element to be present. I know that Selenium has something like but I didn\'t manage to get it to work yet\n\nStack Overflow query: repetitive task automation\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/79909426/automating-repetitive-tasks-with-ruby-and-selenium-webdriver', '7fb28e3ce9ea1fdbaf4ba911e9d2ccfdc37fd10e1d5c95f3009df12037e989c3', 'external:so:79909426', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"ruby\", \"selenium-webdriver\", \"batch-file\", \"send\"], \"query\": \"repetitive task automation\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 12}', '2026-04-26 14:20:00');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_fae20692e745451f82d5141db1bc71da', 'batch_698f9ecf981f47e58ca327423cb21520', 'so:67017379', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/67017379/how-to-wait-for-the-screen-to-catch-up-with-my-vbscript-in-securecrt', 'ND523', '2021-04-09 16:10:00', 'en', 'Need easier way to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate s…', 'Need easier way to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate s…\n\nExtracted demand: Need easier way to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate s…\nUser pain point: I\'m trying to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate some of my more repetitive tasks for me.\nEvidence excerpt: I\'m trying to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate some of my more repetitive tasks for me. Normally, all I have to do is press a couple of keys, but I\'m trying to have a script pre…\nOriginal source title: How to wait for the Screen to catch up with my VBScript in SecureCRT?\n\nStack Overflow Questions auto discovery query: repetitive task automation\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/67017379/how-to-wait-for-the-screen-to-catch-up-with-my-vbscript-in-securecrt', 'f640d94db2975a555fae2a5d2140a81dae352283579940db7c56e76efb993bbb', 'external:so:67017379', 1, 'signal_9b9c0e9cb124491fada88908af9d79a9', NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"vbscript\", \"secure-crt\"], \"query\": \"repetitive task automation\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"auto_extracted\": true, \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"anchor_sentence\": \"I\'m trying to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate some of my more repetitive tasks for me.\", \"extracted_title\": \"Need easier way to write a script for SecureCRT in VBScript that sends keystrokes to automate s…\", \"relevance_score\": 7.3, \"batch_item_index\": 6, \"extraction_query\": \"repetitive task automation\", \"extraction_platform\": \"stack_overflow\"}', '2026-04-26 14:47:47');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_fbbf5263272648e69905577d365fefdb', 'batch_8531cdbfce1d41478ca489f679102efa', 'so:79821111', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/79821111/argocd-applicationset-and-workflow-to-create-ephemeral-environments-from-github', 'luacassus', '2025-11-16 04:58:17', 'en', 'ArgoCD ApplicationSet and Workflow to create ephemeral environments from GitHub branches', 'ArgoCD ApplicationSet and Workflow to create ephemeral environments from GitHub branches\n\nArgoCD ApplicationSet and Workflow to create ephemeral environments from GitHub branches\n\nHow would you rate this GitOps workflow idea with ArgoCD + ApplicationSet + PreSync hooks? In my organization we already use Argo CD for production and staging deployments. We\'re considering giving developers the ability to deploy any code version to temporary test environments aka ephemeral dev namespaces. I would like feedback on the overall design and whether I\'m reinventing the wheel or missing obvious pitfalls. Prerequisites infrastructure repo – GitOps home: ArgoCD Applications, Helm charts, default values. deployment-configuration repo – environment-specific values.yaml files (e.g., image tags). ArgoCD Applications load defaults from infrastructure repo and overrides from deployment-configuration repo. All application services are stateless . Databases (MySQL/Postgres) are separate ArgoCD apps or external services like RDS. Ephemeral environment creation flow Developer pushes code to a branch named dev/{namespace} (or via pull request) GitHub Actions builds the image, pushes it to the registry, uploads assets to CDN, and updates the relevant values.yaml in the deployment-configuration repo with the image tag (e.g. commit sha). ArgoCD ApplicationSet detects the values.yaml and creates a new Application. ArgoCD runs a PreSync hook (or triggers an Argo Workflow) that is fully idempotent . Steps: Create/update Doppler config, write some secrets, create service token to read this config, configure Doppler operator. Create a database + DB user. Create any external resources not part of the application Helm chart. Wait until Doppler Operator creates the managed secret (it syncs every ~30s, so race conditions are possible). Sync Wave -2 : create dependencies that must exist before app deploy (Redis, ConfigMaps, etc.). Sync Wave -1 : If DB is empty: load schema + seed data Run DB migrations and other pre-deployment tasks Sync : finally deploy the application. Update flow Pretty much the same flow as create. Thanks to idempotency we can run exactly the same steps: Developer pushes updates to the same branch. GitHub Actions builds and pushes the image, updates values.yaml. PreSync hook runs again but idempotently skips resource creation. Sync Wave -2: update shared resources if needed. Sync Wave -1: run database migrations and other pre-deployment tasks. Sync: update deployment. Application deletion When the branch is deleted, ApplicationSet removes the Application. PostDelete hook cleans up: deletes Doppler config, drops DB, removes RabbitMQ vhosts, etc. Namespace recovery options Deep Clean Developer manually deletes the ArgoCD Application. PostDelete hook removes all resources. ApplicationSet recreates the namespace from scratch automatically. Soft Clean For instance, a developer wants to have a fresh database ..or database is corrupted (e.g., broken database migrations). Triggered via GitHub Workflow → Argo event → Argo Workflow. Workflow handles: drop DB → restore → reseed. I am also considering adding simple lifecycle management to avoid hundreds of abandoned dev branches consuming cluster resources: Daily GitHub Workflow (cron) scans all dev/{namespace} branches. If a branch has no commits for e.g., 14 days, the workflow commits an update to the corresponding values.yaml to scale replicas down to 0. A new commit instantly bumps replicas back up because the build pipeline updates values.yaml again. If a branch has no commits for 30 days, the workflow deletes the branch and values.yaml entirely. ApplicationSet reacts by deleting the namespace and running the PostDelete cleanup. I\'m Looking for feedback from people who have implemented similar workflows: Does this design follow common ArgoCD patterns? Can you see any major red flags or failure modes I should account for?\n\nStack Overflow query: product feedback workflow\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/79821111/argocd-applicationset-and-workflow-to-create-ephemeral-environments-from-github', 'd2ad4be7dec6b8221e72e31172c3afb58407c60dd27dc6d070797128cffd0fd0', 'external:so:79821111', 1, 'signal_39dd146cfe704f009c683159cf4b24ad', NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"kubernetes\", \"github-actions\", \"cicd\", \"argocd\", \"argo-workflows\"], \"query\": \"product feedback workflow\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"batch_item_index\": 11}', '2026-04-26 14:22:08');
INSERT INTO `raw_signal` VALUES ('signal_fd3ebd9af8d94079897963cdc36a12ae', 'batch_9db6c0e832224c3f81b5d81d3038ebc2', 'so:62192925', 'https://stackoverflow.com/questions/62192925/coredata-has-problems-with-sync-data-to-cloud-on-a-macos-app-due-to-pending-requ', 'metal_man', '2020-06-04 18:56:40', 'en', 'So what is said above - - cannot execute request because there is one pending...', 'So what is said above - - cannot execute request because there is one pending...\n\nExtracted demand: So what is said above - - cannot execute request because there is one pending...\nUser pain point: So what is said above - - cannot execute request because there is one pending...\nEvidence excerpt: I am writing an app for MacOS and main feature will be syncing data to iCloud. All that I\'ve already done is - project with Core-Data and CloudKit options turned on, - created a model and some basic routine to create mo…\nOriginal source title: CoreData has problems with sync data to cloud on a MacOS app due to pending request error\n\nStack Overflow Questions auto discovery query: feature request automation\n\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/62192925/coredata-has-problems-with-sync-data-to-cloud-on-a-macos-app-due-to-pending-requ', 'dcfddf2781f501d648272675795d8e2c5e0bc1336f95c98fe484a03d9b14752c', 'external:so:62192925', 0, NULL, NULL, '{\"tags\": [\"ios\", \"swift\", \"core-data\", \"cloudkit\", \"swift5\"], \"query\": \"feature request automation\", \"has_note\": true, \"platform\": \"stack_overflow\", \"batch_label\": \"Stack Overflow auto discovery\", \"has_content\": true, \"import_type\": \"link\", \"auto_extracted\": true, \"import_channel\": \"manual\", \"anchor_sentence\": \"So what is said above - - cannot execute request because there is one pending...\", \"extracted_title\": \"So what is said above - - cannot execute request because there is one pending...\", \"relevance_score\": 4.5, \"batch_item_index\": 13, \"extraction_query\": \"feature request automation\", \"extra